host Vultr SEA NixOS VPS ai-jail pier (Daylight DC-1 hand) -- Eastern (EDT)
title The rota rotted in a blind spot, and a guard had been grading a cairn
prompt asked about the council rota -- whether its documents are redundant and whether it should be reshaped
think Read the rota before judging it, and the first reading answered a different question than the one asked. Five of the twenty-seven entries are dead paths -- every active-designing one -- so five laps of every cycle would deep-read nothing. That is a fact about the rota worth more than any opinion about its contents.
think Traced why neither dated-path tool caught it. Both prune any directory NAMED seed, an exclusion written for the gitignored root projection. recursion-prompts/seed shares the name and is the loop's own room, so both instruments were blind to it by construction (REDS %122).
think Measured the collateral rather than assuming it. Exactly two directories are named seed, and the second holds twenty-seven dated references. .git and vendor each occur once at the root, so their name match is safe -- which is the difference between a name exclusion that works and one that does not.
think Got the first fix wrong and shipped a leak of 8,543 lines before catching it. I path-anchored grep with --exclude-dir=./seed and read a broken check as success -- grep matches directory names here, so the pattern could never match, and the test I confirmed it with filtered output on a pattern that could never match either. find anchors on -path and was always correct; grep needed the room re-admitted in its own pass.
think Ran the round's guards and one had been red for two days. nib_honesty read the first ten-hex run in the card and called it the Git nib -- and condensing the card on 20260819 moved a cairn row above the nib line, so it was grading a walk-back nib against the nib's ancestor law. A cairn is off main by construction after a deep debride; that is the whole reason it was worth recording.
think Rewrote that guard to own what it uniquely claims -- every advertised hash resolves -- and to CITE remember_git_nib_witness for the nib's own state law rather than copy it. Reachability is named per hash rather than graded, because the two voices in the card cannot keep the same law.
obs Four cairn walk-backs live on no remote at all. The cairn rule promises the departing card stays one git show away, and for those four the promise holds on this machine and nowhere else. Left as a gate rather than crossed -- pushing the pre-debride branches would restore the promise and re-publish tissue a debride deliberately removed, which is Keaton's word.
obs Kept the new guard OUT of the era suite deliberately. That suite promises to be provable on any host, and four local-only cairns mean this one cannot keep that promise yet. Recorded the reason in the guard's own header, where the next person would put it in.
obs The census reads lost=192 against a ceiling of 192 after the repair -- the same number as before it. That sameness is the honest signature of a blind-spot fix rather than a corpus change.
obs REDS crossed its 24,576-byte bound when the two rows landed; row 121 folded to the archive with a pointer, and the ledger reads 20,890.
loom rota_entries=27 dead_before=5 dead_after=0 refs_repointed=11 rooms_blind=1
loom refs_lost=192 ceiling=192 projection_leak_caught=8543 reds_bytes=20890 bound=24576
loom guards_run=6 green=6
file tools/fixtures/dated_path_exclusions.sh name-matched, root-path-anchored, and re-admitted rooms separated, with the reason for each
file tools/fixtures/dated_path_scan.sh the re-admit pass, so the corpus holds the room grep prunes by name
file tools/nib_honesty_witness.rish reads the Git nib field by name, sweeps every advertised hash, names reach rather than grading it
file tools/fixtures/nib_honesty_scan.sh the sweep and its planted floating-nib control
file recursion-prompts/seed/autonomous-loop.seed.md eleven references repointed, every rota entry resolving again
file crux/REDS.md rows 122 and 123 booked and closed, row 121 folded under the bound
recommend check-in (Keaton) the rota now resolves and the reshape question is still open -- worth answering with the reading in hand rather than the reading it replaced. One gate stands named and uncrossed: four cairn walk-backs on no remote.
